00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.330
And to decode a block in a
loop, the loop you just see

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.490
on the screen-- let me zoom in--

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.890
while number of bits
consumed is less than--

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.720
Basically, as long as
you have bits left,

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.580
you try to decode a symbol.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.260
And then in a loop,
basically, you

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:00.550
decode one symbol at a time.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.650
That's prefix-free decoding.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.260
And you might ask, how
