00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:39.600
OK, so last time, we
talked about prefix codes.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.780
So prefix codes are codes,
where no codeword is

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.040
a prefix of another codeword.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.010
And we saw that it really
simplifies the decoding.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.360
And one way of decoding
was this tree-based thing,

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.610
where you start from the root.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.200
You go down the tree
and so on, right?

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.330
I've drawn one of
those here, where

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:57.090
if you see a 1, 0, you go this
way, then you go this way,

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:59.820
and you decode a B. And then
you go back to the root,

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.610
and then you see a 1,
1, 1, so you go to D.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:05.460
You decode D. You
go back to the root.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.710
I won't spend too much time.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.040
I think you might have gotten
some practice in the homework--

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.330
in the quiz.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:15.610
Then, we defined a good code.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.880
I just gave you a thumb
rule, asked you to believe.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.830
We will show this
time why this held,

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:24.347
but we said that a good code
has the length of a symbol.

00:10:24.347 --> 00:10:25.930
The length of the
encoding of a symbol

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.260
is roughly the log of 1 over Px.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:32.320
And then we actually constructed
a code called the Shannon code,

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.820
where the lengths
were actually very

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.175
close to the promised good code.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.870
For Shannon code, we
did the construction.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.130
Construction was very simple.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:45.160
We sorted the symbols
according to their length,

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:49.530
and then we just
basically pick a code word

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.990
that doesn't violate the
prefix free condition.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.510
And I think you had some
homework questions on that.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.540
Then, we did the proof for
why that construction works.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:01.200
Even if it didn't fully follow
